    "scope": "Surviving southeast pronaos corner: exactly three fluted pale Corinthian columns with moulded bases, leafy/corner-volute capitals and the broken L-shaped surviving entablature, with low mapped podium/cella wall fragments and an open destroyed temple interior. No intact cella, roof, full pediment, complete peristyle or ancient full-temple reconstruction. Preserve Tabularium and independent neighboring ruins.",
    "identityBasis": "Exact-QID relation1767603 gives the archaeological extent/axis, not an intact temple shell. Standard PMTiles corner-footing52776559974420 fixes the southeast surviving group. Internal angle +0.580061860533rad, native east/south at runtime heading0. Twelve mapped internal remnant controls are authored; three Portico-side controls outside the relation are independent. Column centers, heights, low remnant heights and their local podium levels are picture-led approximations.",
    "heightBasis": "About15.2m column including base/capital; surviving entablature about17.8m above the corner footing. Relative proportions are picture-led; detailed conservation dimensions are not claimed. The inspected pictures guide deep shaft flutes, layered round bases, two leafy capital rows/corner volutes, concave abaci, the broken L-shaped fascia/cornice and taller rough entablature core. Fine sacrifice reliefs, letters, repair pins and exact ancient carving are simplified.",
    "terrainBasis": "Reuse pinned standard Rome PMTiles/Mapzen extract from temple_of_portunus; sample native six-meter grid at the current anchor. One local level footing supports the small three-column corner, with a buried base; other low remnants follow their local coarse grade. Retain courtyard terrain, water and independent neighboring buildings. No broad fabricated raised temple platform. Coarse ground does not resolve excavation walls or original temple paving; local threshold levels and remnant heights remain approximate.",
    "constructionStatus": "continuous-authoring-and-inspection"
  },
